Save93 / Whiterun exterior / GetAt to GetWorldSpace replication / 2026-11-09

Implementation under test
- GameplayTrace-only mode. The stock tasklet must be at the head of the VM's existing task queue, with the same stock native phase, render frame and remaining budget. Only a stock FormList.GetAt return from DynDOLOD ObjectEnabler can qualify the following stock ObjectReference.GetWorldSpace for immediate execution. The engine executes the original tasklet, object-lock and native-result paths.
- At most one tasklet slice and one newly eligible native call per render frame. The admission deadline is bounded by the original phase budget and 0.25 ms. A measured slice over 0.50 ms stops further attempts for the trial. This is not a preemptive runtime cap.
- y/Y records the source and returned VM handles after successful stock marshalling. The analysis compares results to off observations of the same source handle after exterior arrival in the same game process. It checks stock GetAt return -> tasklet accept -> same-thread GetWorldSpace dispatch/return, and correlates the original return lock with recorded ownership. It does not resolve or synthesize an extra Papyrus result.
- No PEX changes. Production AdaptivePapyrusBudget sources have no changes from this replication.

Conditions and aborted runs
- Skyrim AE 1.6.1170.0, SSE Display Tweaks 0.5.16 with 42 FPS gameplay cap and dynamic VM budget, 60 FPS loading cap. Papyrus Tweaks NG DLL loaded, with bSpeedUpNativeCalls=false in its winning config.
- Verified original Save93 ESS SHA256 87C181889BB60A565C327FF0AA0B1B6F46D568AC0EB29C022925A3912742277D and SKSE cosave SHA256 5EE67E98B488FAE5BD5C1E5A9A87DA9D92522D480255F2F1BA84E6FB80F1B0AA.
- Two targeted launches with the original frame generation setting aborted before any measured exterior return. A third launch using the exact prior successful DLL (SHA256 565AA7B3F67850A08AC2BD252D9120C822A84608846433CA7A192F23F8FEE458) reproduced the same Bannered Mare staging freeze. The main thread stack snapshots for the second targeted launch and control matched from ntdll delay through Skyrim, Engine Fixes, SkyrimUpscaler and Community Shaders. These snapshots do not uniquely attribute cause.
- For subsequent A/B launches only the disposable test mod overrode SkyrimUpscaler.ini mEnableFrameGeneration=false and mFrameGenType=0 in both arms. The same Save93, DynDOLOD files and Display Tweaks configuration were used. Original winning Upscaler config hash 3CF1A335E01731D2A40A884D7A2335AF55009B29B06DB739EB397566F299677E; temporary override hash 5A090355F6D3C9DCF0E03BE1315E474AF07D9DBCD8803D6AFFF7FDC472311CEB.
- Measured runs entered Bannered Mare (0001605E) and waited for 3 x 0.5 s at the target cadence before returning to WhiterunWorld (0001A27F). The first staging also required 5 s of stable frames in Save93. The 32 response probes per trial are Utility.Wait(0.01) starting about one second after arrival. Each process starts from the original Save93 copy. In-session scene state carries from one trial to the next.
- First frame-generation-off DLL SHA256 16EBAF946591E8483FE4D0356B6223F66A583E03C4270B7A699E883FFECAC4F0. Eight complete A/B trials survived. The game had a Windows-reported execute access violation 0xc0000005 in an unknown module just after the ninth window opened (disabled; before recorded arrival). Cause unproven. That incomplete window is excluded. The second launch changes the test length and ordering only, building SHA256 B88A2F305A7126A58181347A024F3881A219B5928FE23E3991CFD3B23A48D51F.
- Render percentiles use engine-count-validated PresentMon intervals. The steady interval is the last two seconds. Timing during arrival fluctuates even though the gameplay cap is 42. The local sampled FPS for promotions uses engine frames around +/-250 ms, independently of the VM timing gate.

Prior-render-profile bottleneck readback
- Reanalyzed the four earlier complete windows in cell-42-continuation-budget-ab. The last DynDOLOD stack spent 840.827 to 1085.271 ms in aggregate between GetAt native return and VM frame completion. GetWorldSpace Q->P was 210.987 to 334.542 ms across those same stacks. The two intervals are different stages.
- The GetAt return was blocked by the script-instance lock. Across the four prior tails, 190 observed failed acquisition attempts were matched by lock token to an existing DynDOLOD owner at the sample point (126 OnCellAttach, 64 OnCellDetach). This is an attempt count, not the number of distinct calls. The narrow continuation starts after GetAt has already completed its return/lock handoff.
- xmake built APBGameplayTrace and AdaptivePapyrusBudget successfully. xmake run budget_policy_tests passed. Analyzer synthetic checks covered wrong frame, wrong stack, wrong thread, missing result evidence and prior lock release. The prior capture still analyzes without replication flags.

