Interpretation and cleanup
- All seven observed immediate GetWorldSpace calls matched the off result for the same input handle and had a matching live return-lock owner. The matched input was one reference across the measured launches. The three promotions of the last overall stack took place around 41.872, 42.020, and 43.714 local engine FPS. Other promoted calls include post-loading cadence above 45 FPS.
- The shorter post-arrival paired times do not support an aggregate causal benefit. The median paired delta among actual-activation pairs was -12.985 ms. Among enabled pairs without any promotion it was -49.321 ms. Pooled response p95 slightly increased and request-to-last-stack did not consistently improve. Tail identity varied between DynDOLOD and other scripts, and the total interval includes cell loading.
- The feature remains in the test DLL because aggregate benefit, broad return equivalence, and crash attribution were not established. Retaining stock object lock semantics is necessary. The next GetWorldSpace begins after the separate GetAt return-lock delay.
- The reverse launch completed all eight trials and PresentMon exited successfully. After both launches the MO2 selection was restored to TKL - MUNG ADDON - SPS Test and the temporary test mod and profile were archived. The original Save93 and original SkyrimUpscaler.ini hashes matched the recorded values.
- Raw captures: build/gameplay-trace/cell-42-continuation-replication-no-fg and build/gameplay-trace/cell-42-continuation-replication-no-fg-reverse.
